      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 40,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p14_b68",
      "text": "\u2022 Feature Extraction: Take a pre-trained language model, denoted as f\u03b8pre(x) (e.g., LLaMA-8B) and extract the\nlast-layer hidden states (embeddings) for the input data x. For the LLaMA-8B model, these extracted features have a\ndimension of d = 4096.\n",
      "bbox": [
        66.9,
        517.38,
        541.44,
        551.49
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        267,
        2069,
        2165,
        2205
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 248,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p14_b69",
      "text": "\u2022 Convex Reformulation (cvxNN): Instead of a standard neural network head, COALA stacks a convex neural network\n(cvxNN) on top of these d = 4096 extracted features. This network, denoted as gcvx\n",
      "bbox": [
        66.9,
        562.28,
        541.69,
        584.24
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        267,
        2249,
        2166,
        2336
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 194,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p14_b70",
      "text": "\u03981,\u03b82, serves as a binary preference\nclassifier.\n",
      "bbox": [
        75.37,
        574.24,
        541.44,
        596.19
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        301,
        2296,
        2165,
