      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 48,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p14_b71",
      "text": "\u2022 Solving with CRONOS: We train this cvxNN by solving the convex optimization problem (Equation 4) using the\nCRONOS algorithm. CRONOS uses the Alternating Direction Method of Multipliers (ADMM) to efficiently solve this\nhigh-dimensional problem on a GPU. The output of this phase are the proven optimal weights for the convex layers:\n(\u03981, \u03b82).\n",
      "bbox": [
